Native headless merge research prototype

HeadlessProgramMergeManager.java adapts the orchestration
of Ghidra 12.1.2 MergeManager, developed by the National Security
Agency and distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (APACHE-2.0.txt).
The subclass is modified for test-only synchronous headless execution and refuses
unresolved conflicts. The stock ProgramMultiUserMergeManager superclass selects
and orders the native resolvers; the subclass does not implement merge categories.

The proof extracts additional source files from the explicitly supplied Ghidra
installation. It verifies their pinned hashes and changes the headless
entry guards and display seams in its disposable compilation directory. A
separately recorded MemoryMergeManager compatibility patch corrects unchanged
null comment handling and symmetric delete-versus-update conflict detection.
Those generated sources retain their original license headers. No modified
Ghidra JAR or extracted upstream source is distributed in this fixture directory.
